---
description: "Prints registration details for one named skill, or a discovery listing of every registered skill when none is named."
alwaysApply: false
---

## Purpose

Print a registered skill's own registration details, or list every registered skill, on request.

## When to use

- A skill identifier is declared: show that one skill's Name, Description, Dependencies,
  Version, Usage, and Example.
- No skill identifier is declared: list every registered skill's Name, Usage, and a copy-able
  Help command.
- Confirming a skill exists, or discovering what a skill's exact invocation syntax is, before
  using it.

## When not to use

- Do not use to validate a skill file's authoring correctness; use
  `.highway/tools/validate-skill.sh <skill-dir>` instead.
- Do not use to browse skill overlap or dependency graphs; that is
  `.highway/catalog/index.json`'s `overlap_flags` field, read directly.

## Inputs

- The optional declared skill identifier — the same, full agent-facing id as the target
  skill's directory name under `.highway/skills/` (e.g. `highway-help`), not a bare or
  abbreviated form.
- `.highway/catalog/index.json`, generated by `.highway/tools/generate-catalog.sh` — read for
  All-Skills mode, and to resolve a declared identifier to its `source_path` and `id` for
  Single-Skill mode [AS-4: .highway/catalog/index.json].
- The target skill's own `.highway/skills/<id>/SKILL.md` frontmatter (`description`, `usage`,
  `metadata.version`, `metadata.dependencies`) and `## Example` body section, for Single-Skill
  mode. Frontmatter `name` is validated to equal `<id>` exactly, but `Name:` below is still read
  from the catalog `id`, never frontmatter `name` directly — see Outputs below.

## Outputs

Satisfies `X1.1`, `X1.2`, `X1.3` and `X5.1` of the Highway Experience Standard.

- Single-Skill mode: exactly six labeled lines — `Name:`, `Description:`, `Dependencies:`,
  `Version:`, `Usage:`, `Example:` — in that order, per the help output contract defined by
  feature 009 (skill id namespace alignment).
  `Name:` is the resolved catalog `id`, read verbatim — already the full agent-facing
  identifier, so no prefix is concatenated. `Example:` presents its invocation value as an
  inline code span (backtick-wrapped), containing only the runnable invocation.
  `Dependencies:` reads `none` when `metadata.dependencies` is empty, otherwise a
  comma-separated `path@version` list.
- All-Skills mode: one `Name:`/`Usage:`/`Help: /highway-help <id>` block per catalog entry, in
  catalog order, one entry per registered skill, or the exact line
  `No skills are registered yet.` when the catalog is empty. `Name:` is resolved the same way as
  Single-Skill mode.
- Listing all skills reads the whole catalog once: cost is O(n), where n is the number of
  registered skill entries.

## Verification

This self-check exercises `X1.1`, `X1.2`, `X1.3` and `X5.1`.

- Run `.highway/tools/validate-skill.sh .highway/skills/highway-help` and confirm exit 0.
- Request help for `highway-help` itself and confirm the response has exactly six fields in the
  order above, with a non-blank value on every line, `Name: highway-help`, and an `Example:`
  value wrapped in inline code.
- Request help with no identifier declared and confirm one block per entry currently in
  `.highway/catalog/index.json`, matching entry count exactly, each with a `Help:` line reading
  `/highway-help <id>`.
- See the checked scenarios recorded by feature 009 (skill id namespace alignment) for the
  full set.

## Error Handling

- Declared identifier matches no entry in `.highway/catalog/index.json`: abort and print exactly
  `ERROR: no skill registered with id '<declared-id>'`; do not fall back to the All-Skills
  listing.
- No skill identifier declared and the catalog has zero entries: abort the listing and print
  exactly `No skills are registered yet.`; do not print an empty table.
- Catalog file `.highway/catalog/index.json` is missing or unreadable: abort and instruct the
  caller to run `.highway/tools/generate-catalog.sh` first.

## Example

`/highway-help highway-help`

```text
Name: highway-help
Description: Prints registration details for one named skill, or a discovery listing of every registered skill when none is named.
Dependencies: none
Version: 3.0.3
Usage: Invoke as `/highway-help` for all skills, or `/highway-help <skill-id>` for one named skill's registration details.
Example: `/highway-help highway-help`
```
